  "title": "Welcome to the Arduino Christmas Calendar 🎄",
  "icon": "🎄",
  "markdown": "Behind every door hides a new surprise! Each day until Christmas, you open a door and get a **new exercise**, often with a **new component** to explore. Some days are quick, others are a bit more of a challenge, and they all build on what you learned the day before.\n\nNo peeking ahead! 🎅\n\n## What Is the UNO Q?\n\nThe UNO Q has **two brains** on one board:\n\n- A **Linux computer** that runs Python and can host web pages.\n- A **microcontroller** that runs Arduino sketches and controls LEDs, buttons, sensors and motors.\n\nThe two talk to each other through the **Bridge**. You'll get to know both of them during the calendar.\n\n## Get Ready\n\n1. Download and install **Arduino App Lab** from [arduino.cc/en/software](https://www.arduino.cc/en/software).\n2. Connect the UNO Q to your computer with the USB-C cable.\n3. Open Arduino App Lab and follow the steps to set up your board.\n\n## Import an App\n\nEvery day has a **Download App** button that gives you a `.zip` file. To import it:\n\n1. Open any App in Arduino App Lab.\n2. Select the arrow (**▼**) next to the App name near the top left corner.\n3. Select **Import App**.\n4. Drag and drop the `.zip` file into the import area, or select **Import from computer**.\n5. Select **Open**, then click **Run**.\n\n## How Each Day Works\n\nEvery door has the same simple steps:\n\n- **You Need:** the parts for the day.\n- **Connect:** how to wire everything up.\n- **Run:** how to start the App.\n- **How It Works:** what is going on behind the scenes.\n\nReady? Close this page and open **door number 1**! 🎁",
