  "title": "Python Elf 🧝",
  "icon": "🧝",
  "markdown": "The UNO Q has two brains: a Linux computer running Python, and a microcontroller running the sketch. In this App, a little Python elf tells the microcontroller when to blink the built-in LED, using the **Bridge**.\n\n## You Need\n\n- Arduino UNO Q\n\n## Connect\n\nNothing to connect! The LED is already on the board.\n\n## Run\n\n1. Import the App into Arduino App Lab.\n2. Click **Run**.\n3. The LED blinks every second, and the Python console shows `Elf says: LED ON / OFF`.\n\n## How It Works\n\n- `sketch.ino` registers a function called `set_led` with `Bridge.provide()`.\n- `main.py` calls it with `Bridge.call(\"set_led\", True/False)`.",
  "zip": "../zips/day-06-python-elf.zip"
